      <div type="clause" n="16">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 16</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>LX. Se ðe ðeof ofslihð, se mot gecyðan mid aðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hine synnigne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.8"/> ofsloge, nalles<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.9-2"/> ða gegildan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>Se ðe þeof ofslehð, he mot geceþan mit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.1"/> aþe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hine synnigne ofsloge, nalles þa gegildanum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="96" ed="#liebermann"/>Se ðe ðeof ofslihð, se mot gecyþan mid his aðe, ðæt he hine synnigne ofsloge, nallæs ða gegildan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ðeofslæge. Se ðe ðeof ofslihð, se mot gecyþan mid aðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hine scyldig ofslóge, nalles ða gyldan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="16" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui furem occiderit, debet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.9"/> inueritare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.10"/> cum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.11"/> iuramento, quod illum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.12"/> culpabilem (et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.13"/> de uita forisfactum) occidisset<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_16.lnote.oe.14"/>, et non soluat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="40" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðeofslæge.] Se ðe ðeof ofslihð, se<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Ine_16.attnote.fn.10"/> mot gecyðan mid aðe<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Ine_16.attnote.fn.14"/> þæt he hine synnigne<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#Ine_16.attnote.fn.15"/> ofsloge, nalles ða gegildan<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#Ine_16.attnote.fn.16"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="16" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="382" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LX} Se ðe ðeof ofslihð, se mot gecyðan mid aðe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hine synnigne ofsloge; nalles ða gegildan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="97" ed="#liebermann"/>Wer einen [handhaften<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_16.lnote.de.1"/>] Dieb<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_16.lnote.de.2"/> erschlägt, der darf [wenn deshalb verklagt,] durch (seinen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_16.lnote.de.3"/>) Eid erweisen, dass er ihn als Schuldigen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_16.lnote.de.4"/> erschlagen habe, keineswegs die Gildegenossen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_16.lnote.de.5"/> [des Todten gelangen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_16.lnote.de.6"/> zum Beweise].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Whoever slays a [red-handed] thief may [if accused on that account] prove by (his) oath that he slew him as a guilty man; by no means [do] the guild-brothers [of the dead man get to the proof].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="41" ed="#attenborough"/>He who kills a thief shall be allowed to declare on oath that the man he slew was guilty. The associates<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_16.attnote.n.1"/> of the slain man shall not be allowed to proceed to an oath<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_16.attnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="401" ed="#whitelock"/>He who slays a thief may declare with an oath that he slew him as a guilty man, by no means the associates.<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_16.whinote.n.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="383" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>He who kills a thief may declare with an oath that he killed him because he was [found] guilty [in the act]; this does not apply to his associates.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><label>see</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-25">Af El 25</ref> <quote>See Swerian §4, MP §25.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_21">Ine 21</ref> <quote>Compare §20.1 and §35.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_35">Ine 35</ref> <quote>Compare §20.1 and §35.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><label>see</label> <ref target="clause:Swer_4">Swer 4</ref> <quote>See Swerian §4, MP §25.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="385"><ref target="clause:Ine_21">Ine 21</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="401"><ref target="clause:Ine_35">Ine 35</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">probare <hi rend="italic">fügen zu Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">probare added by Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in ueritate <hi rend="italic">T Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in ueritate T Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">per iuramentum <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">per iuramentum Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ipsum <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ipsum Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et de u. f. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et de u. f. lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">occidit <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">occidit Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> gegildan</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read gegildan</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scyldig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scyldig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ nales ða gegyldan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ nales ða gegyldan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wiederholt 21. 35. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> handhaft 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Repeated in 21. 35. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> handhaft 11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Aus 21 und Erwähnung der Gilde folgt keineswegs, ein Fremder sei zunächst gemeint</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">From 21 and the mention of the guild it by no means follows that a stranger is primarily meant</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Unnötiger Zusatz H’s</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Unnecessary addition by H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B modernisiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B modernises</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht Infin., wie Price, Toller annehmen, aus Q, der <hi rend="italic">u.</hi> 21 richtig. — B modernisiert; Bu verderbt. — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Genossenschaft 3b. Es ist nicht an eine spezifisch städtische Einrichtung zu denken</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not an infin., as Price and Toller assume on the basis of Q, who has it right <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 21. — B modernises; Bu corrupt. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Genossenschaft 3b. A specifically urban institution is not to be thought of</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_16.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">71</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diese Ergänzung Kemble’s (in <hi rend="italic">Brit. review</hi> 1841, 54. 84; dann <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> I 46. II 84) fand fast allgemein Beistimmung (ausser Waitz <hi rend="italic">Dt. Verf. G.</hi> I 436 = 1880 S. 464). Nicht hierher gehört die Reinigung amtlich Hingerichteter (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5) durch Genossen. — Hinzuzudenken ist aus Ine 21, 1, dass der Totschlag von Anfang an nicht verheimlicht wurde. — Keiner Widerlegung bedarf Thorpes Idee, Ine treffe den Mörder eines Diebsgenossen, der letzterem Beute abnehmen und durch dessen Anzeige Meldelohn verdienen wolle</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This supplement of Kemble’s (in <hi rend="italic">Brit. review</hi> 1841, 54. 84; then <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> I 46. II 84) has met with almost universal agreement (except for Waitz <hi rend="italic">Dt. Verf. G.</hi> I 436 = 1880 p. 464). The exculpation by associates of men officially executed (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5) does not belong here. — It is to be understood from Ine 21, 1 that the killing was not concealed from the outset. — Thorpe’s idea, that Ine is dealing with the slayer of a fellow thief who wanted to take the booty from the latter and earn an informer’s reward by denouncing him, needs no refutation</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_16.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>se</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">he</hi>. Bu.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 10 is printed 2 times on the page (14, 16), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_16.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>aðe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">his aðe</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_16.attnote.fn.15" n="15" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>synnigne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">scyldig</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_16.attnote.fn.16" n="16" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>gegildan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gyldan</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_16.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">185</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Lit. ‘those associated with him in payment’ (of the wergeld). The word probably refers primarily to relatives (cf. cap. 74 § 2), though in Alf. cap. 27 it would seem to be otherwise. See B. and T. for other references.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_16.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">185</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">In order to exculpate him (cf. cap. 21 and 21 § 1 below).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_16.whinote.n.5" n="5" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">401</biblScope></bibl><label>associates</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">This obscure statement probably means that the thief’s associates have no right to swear to his innocence. These associates <hi rend="italic">(gegildan)</hi> have been variously interpreted. Liebermann thinks that already we have a guild like that in VI Athelstan (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> No. 37); he notes that in Inc 21, 21.1, the term seems to interchange with “kinsmen”, but suggests that the latter word is being used widely. But it may be <hi rend="italic">gegildan</hi> which is vague, denoting “those associated with him in payment” (Attenborough), primarily his kinsmen, <hi rend="italic">see</hi> p. 365.</seg></note>
      </div>
